1
00:00:00,133 --> 00:00:02,733
很多人对喝茶最大的误解是
The biggest misconception people have about drinking tea

2
00:00:02,966 --> 00:00:04,700
以为茶是一种饮料
They think tea is a drink

3
00:00:04,833 --> 00:00:05,633
不是
It's not

4
00:00:05,966 --> 00:00:07,766
在中国人的关系里
In Chinese relationships

5
00:00:07,766 --> 00:00:10,433
茶很多时候不是用来解渴的
Tea is often not for quenching thirst

6
00:00:10,600 --> 00:00:12,333
它是用来试探距离的
It's used to test the distance between people

7
00:00:12,500 --> 00:00:14,966
也是用来给关系报价的
And to put a price on a relationship

8
00:00:15,100 --> 00:00:18,233
你以为别人叫你喝茶是因为口渴
You think someone invited you for tea because they're thirsty

9
00:00:18,566 --> 00:00:21,333
但很多时候真正重要的不是那杯茶
But often what really matters isn't the tea

10
00:00:21,633 --> 00:00:23,933
而是你愿不愿意坐下来
It's whether you're willing to sit down

11
00:00:24,133 --> 00:00:25,900
愿不愿意给对方时间
Willing to give them your time

12
00:00:26,100 --> 00:00:27,933
愿不愿意听他把话说完
Willing to hear them out

13
00:00:28,033 --> 00:00:30,966
一杯茶最厉害的地方就在这里
This is the real power of a cup of tea

14
00:00:30,966 --> 00:00:32,933
它不会像钱那样直接
It's not as direct as money

15
00:00:33,166 --> 00:00:35,000
也不会像合同那样冰冷
Nor as cold as a contract

16
00:00:35,166 --> 00:00:36,233
它很温和
It's gentle

17
00:00:36,500 --> 00:00:37,366
很体面
Dignified

18
00:00:37,600 --> 00:00:39,833
甚至看起来什么都没发生
It even looks like nothing happened at all

19
00:00:40,000 --> 00:00:44,366
但一段关系的远近轻重值不值得继续
But the closeness weight and worthiness of a relationship

20
00:00:44,533 --> 00:00:47,166
往往就在这一杯茶里被重新估价
Often gets reassessed right there in that cup of tea

21
00:00:47,400 --> 00:00:50,000
所以这条视频不讲茶文化
So this video isn't about tea culture

22
00:00:50,166 --> 00:00:51,900
也不讲茶叶知识
Nor tea knowledge

23
00:00:52,033 --> 00:00:54,033
只讲一个反直觉的判断
Just one counterintuitive observation

24
00:00:54,233 --> 00:00:55,633
茶不是饮料
Tea is not a drink

25
00:00:55,900 --> 00:00:58,633
茶是中国人最温和的一种社交货币
Tea is the gentlest form of social currency in China

26
00:00:58,766 --> 00:01:01,233
它真正交换的不是茶水
What it really exchanges isn't tea

27
00:01:01,333 --> 00:01:04,633
而是时间面子信任和人情
But time face trust and favors

28
00:01:04,733 --> 00:01:05,900
你有没有发现
Have you noticed

29
00:01:06,100 --> 00:01:08,533
中国人很多话不会直接说
Chinese people often don't say things directly

30
00:01:08,766 --> 00:01:09,766
想谈合作
When they want to discuss a deal

31
00:01:09,966 --> 00:01:11,366
不一定先发方案
They might not start with a proposal

32
00:01:11,533 --> 00:01:12,600
可能先说
They might say

33
00:01:12,933 --> 00:01:14,100
有空喝杯茶
Let's grab some tea when you're free

34
00:01:14,333 --> 00:01:15,733
想缓和关系
When they want to ease tension

35
00:01:15,900 --> 00:01:17,033
不一定先道歉
They might not apologize first

36
00:01:17,300 --> 00:01:18,366
可能先说
They might say

37
00:01:18,633 --> 00:01:20,700
来坐坐泡壶茶
Come sit down let's brew some tea

38
00:01:20,933 --> 00:01:22,000
想请人帮忙
When they need a favor

39
00:01:22,300 --> 00:01:23,700
不一定一上来就开口
They might not ask right away

40
00:01:23,900 --> 00:01:25,633
可能先把茶杯推过去
They might slide the teacup over first

41
00:01:25,800 --> 00:01:27,000
先寒暄几句
Make some small talk

42
00:01:27,200 --> 00:01:28,600
先问最近怎么样
Ask how you've been

43
00:01:28,800 --> 00:01:30,566
这套动作看起来很绕
This routine seems roundabout

44
00:01:30,800 --> 00:01:32,133
但它不是没有用
But it's not pointless

45
00:01:32,333 --> 00:01:34,833
它是在降低关系里的尴尬成本
It reduces the awkwardness cost in relationships

46
00:01:35,000 --> 00:01:38,300
有些话太直接会让人没法接
Some things are too direct and leave people no room to respond

47
00:01:38,300 --> 00:01:39,100
比如
Like

48
00:01:39,300 --> 00:01:40,333
你能不能帮我
Can you help me

49
00:01:40,500 --> 00:01:42,000
你愿不愿意站我这边
Will you take my side

50
00:01:42,133 --> 00:01:43,400
你到底认不认可我
Do you actually respect me

51
00:01:43,600 --> 00:01:45,400
这类话一旦说出口
Once words like these are spoken

52
00:01:45,600 --> 00:01:46,833
对方要么答应
The other person either agrees

53
00:01:47,033 --> 00:01:48,100
要么拒绝
Or refuses

54
00:01:48,233 --> 00:01:49,566
场面就变硬了
And the situation turns stiff

55
00:01:49,700 --> 00:01:53,333
而茶的作用就是给双方一个缓冲区
Tea creates a buffer zone for both sides

56
00:01:53,433 --> 00:01:54,800
你可以先坐下来
You can sit down first

57
00:01:54,933 --> 00:01:55,833
先喝一口
Take a sip first

58
00:01:56,033 --> 00:02:00,133
先聊天气聊近况聊孩子聊工作
Talk about the weather recent life kids work

59
00:02:00,333 --> 00:02:02,300
真正的事慢慢浮出来
The real issue surfaces gradually

60
00:02:02,433 --> 00:02:04,133
这就是茶的第一层作用
This is tea's first function

61
00:02:04,300 --> 00:02:05,600
它不是解决问题
It doesn't solve problems

62
00:02:05,933 --> 00:02:08,000
它是让问题有机会被说出来
It gives problems a chance to be voiced

63
00:02:08,166 --> 00:02:09,100
你会发现
You'll find

64
00:02:09,233 --> 00:02:11,733
很多关系最怕的不是没结果
The worst thing in a relationship isn't having no outcome

65
00:02:11,900 --> 00:02:14,133
而是连坐下来谈的资格都没有
It's not even having the right to sit down and talk

66
00:02:14,333 --> 00:02:16,000
别人愿意请你喝茶
When someone invites you for tea

67
00:02:16,200 --> 00:02:17,566
至少说明一件事
It means at least one thing

68
00:02:17,733 --> 00:02:19,733
这段关系还没有被直接关闭
This relationship hasn't been shut down yet

69
00:02:19,900 --> 00:02:21,400
你愿意去喝这杯茶
If you're willing to go

70
00:02:21,633 --> 00:02:23,400
也等于在表达
That's also a statement

71
00:02:23,600 --> 00:02:25,833
我还愿意给这段关系一点时间
I'm still willing to give this relationship some time

72
00:02:26,000 --> 00:02:28,966
所以一杯茶的价格不在茶叶上
So the price of tea isn't in the leaves

73
00:02:29,133 --> 00:02:30,233
在时间上
It's in the time

74
00:02:30,433 --> 00:02:33,433
一个真正忙的人愿意给你半小时
A truly busy person giving you half an hour

75
00:02:33,700 --> 00:02:35,700
这半小时本身就是成本
Those thirty minutes are a cost in themselves

76
00:02:35,800 --> 00:02:37,533
一个不缺饭局的人
Someone who never lacks dinner invitations

77
00:02:37,566 --> 00:02:39,233
愿意坐下来听你说完
Sitting down to hear you out

78
00:02:39,400 --> 00:02:41,133
这件事本身就是信号
That act itself is a signal

79
00:02:41,300 --> 00:02:44,233
关系里最贵的往往不是钱
The most expensive thing in relationships isn't money

80
00:02:44,433 --> 00:02:47,033
而是一个人愿意把注意力放在你身上
It's someone willing to give you their full attention

81
00:02:47,200 --> 00:02:48,933
所以茶不是饮料
So tea isn't a drink

82
00:02:49,100 --> 00:02:50,800
茶是一种很轻的邀请
It's a very light invitation

83
00:02:50,933 --> 00:02:52,566
也是一种很重的信号
And a very heavy signal

84
00:02:52,700 --> 00:02:54,900
但茶只交换时间还不够
But exchanging just time isn't enough

85
00:02:55,100 --> 00:02:57,800
中国人的茶桌上真正流动的
What really flows on Chinese tea tables

86
00:02:57,833 --> 00:02:59,033
往往是面子
Is often face

87
00:02:59,166 --> 00:03:00,400
你想一个场景
Picture a scene

88
00:03:00,700 --> 00:03:01,766
别人给你倒茶
Someone pours you tea

89
00:03:02,033 --> 00:03:03,800
你会不会完全无感
Would you feel nothing at all

90
00:03:03,966 --> 00:03:04,966
一般不会
Probably not

91
00:03:05,133 --> 00:03:06,166
你可能会说
You might say

92
00:03:06,333 --> 00:03:07,133
谢谢
Thanks

93
00:03:07,233 --> 00:03:08,766
你可能会轻敲桌面
You might tap the table lightly

94
00:03:08,900 --> 00:03:10,833
你可能会把杯子往前推一点
You might nudge your cup forward

95
00:03:11,000 --> 00:03:12,433
这些动作很小
These gestures are tiny

96
00:03:12,633 --> 00:03:15,100
但它们都在表达一种关系秩序
But they all express a social hierarchy

97
00:03:15,333 --> 00:03:16,366
谁先倒
Who pours first

98
00:03:16,633 --> 00:03:17,533
倒给谁
Who gets poured for

99
00:03:17,766 --> 00:03:18,633
倒多少
How much to pour

100
00:03:18,833 --> 00:03:20,300
杯子放在哪里
Where to place the cup

101
00:03:20,500 --> 00:03:21,433
谁坐主位
Who takes the seat of honor

102
00:03:21,633 --> 00:03:22,933
谁先开口
Who speaks first

103
00:03:23,100 --> 00:03:25,000
这些细节看起来像礼貌
These details look like politeness

104
00:03:25,300 --> 00:03:27,233
其实是在给关系排座次
They're actually ranking the relationship

105
00:03:27,366 --> 00:03:28,633
更微妙的是
What's more subtle

106
00:03:28,900 --> 00:03:30,600
茶桌上的很多付出
Many gestures at the tea table

107
00:03:30,833 --> 00:03:32,933
不会被直接说成交易
Are never openly called transactions

108
00:03:33,033 --> 00:03:34,700
你送对方一盒茶
You gift someone a box of tea

109
00:03:35,000 --> 00:03:36,033
你不会说
You won't say

110
00:03:36,300 --> 00:03:39,033
这盒茶价值多少所以你欠我多少
This tea is worth this much so you owe me this much

111
00:03:39,233 --> 00:03:40,333
那样太难看
That would be too ugly

112
00:03:40,500 --> 00:03:42,166
但对方心里会知道
But the other person knows

113
00:03:42,366 --> 00:03:43,500
你花了心思
You put in thought

114
00:03:43,600 --> 00:03:44,833
你给了面子
You gave them face

115
00:03:44,933 --> 00:03:46,633
你把这段关系当回事
You took this relationship seriously

116
00:03:46,833 --> 00:03:48,933
这就是茶和钱最大的区别
This is the biggest difference between tea and money

117
00:03:49,166 --> 00:03:50,133
钱太直
Money is too blunt

118
00:03:50,333 --> 00:03:51,800
直到容易伤人
So blunt it can hurt people

119
00:03:52,000 --> 00:03:53,133
茶比较软
Tea is softer

120
00:03:53,300 --> 00:03:55,500
软到可以让双方都保留体面
Soft enough to let both sides keep their dignity

121
00:03:55,633 --> 00:03:58,166
所以茶在中国人的社交里
So in Chinese social life tea

122
00:03:58,333 --> 00:04:00,766
经常承担一种很特殊的功能
Often serves a very special function

123
00:04:00,900 --> 00:04:03,166
它让利益交换看起来不像利益交换
It makes exchanges of interest not look like exchanges

124
00:04:03,366 --> 00:04:05,800
让请求看起来不像请求
Makes requests not look like requests

125
00:04:05,933 --> 00:04:07,800
让示好看起来不像讨好
Makes gestures of goodwill not look like flattery

126
00:04:07,966 --> 00:04:10,333
让拒绝也不至于太难堪
Makes rejection not too humiliating

127
00:04:10,533 --> 00:04:12,166
比如别人请你喝茶
For example someone invites you for tea

128
00:04:12,400 --> 00:04:13,300
你去了
You go

129
00:04:13,500 --> 00:04:14,900
说明你愿意给面子
That means you're willing to give face

130
00:04:15,000 --> 00:04:16,033
你一直推
You keep declining

131
00:04:16,300 --> 00:04:18,033
对方也大概明白
And the other person gets the hint

132
00:04:18,200 --> 00:04:19,933
这段关系还没到那个程度
This relationship hasn't reached that level yet

133
00:04:20,133 --> 00:04:21,966
再比如别人送你茶
Or someone gifts you tea

134
00:04:22,233 --> 00:04:23,200
你收下了
You accept it

135
00:04:23,333 --> 00:04:25,100
这不是简单拿了一件礼物
It's not just receiving a gift

136
00:04:25,233 --> 00:04:26,900
它可能意味着
It might mean

137
00:04:27,033 --> 00:04:28,900
你接受了对方的善意
You accepted their goodwill

138
00:04:29,000 --> 00:04:31,566
也默认这段关系以后可以继续往来
And tacitly agreed this relationship can continue

139
00:04:31,733 --> 00:04:32,700
你不收
You don't accept

140
00:04:32,833 --> 00:04:34,300
也不一定是嫌弃茶
It's not necessarily that you dislike the tea

141
00:04:34,600 --> 00:04:36,600
可能是在告诉对方
You might be telling them

142
00:04:36,833 --> 00:04:38,600
这层关系不能再往前走了
This relationship shouldn't go any further

143
00:04:38,800 --> 00:04:41,200
所以茶最有意思的地方在于
The most fascinating thing about tea

144
00:04:41,533 --> 00:04:43,100
它很少明码标价
Is that it's rarely price-tagged

145
00:04:43,200 --> 00:04:45,033
但所有人都在心里估价
But everyone is pricing it in their head

146
00:04:45,200 --> 00:04:46,933
这就是社交货币的特点
That's the nature of social currency

147
00:04:47,033 --> 00:04:48,933
它不一定能直接换钱
It might not convert directly to cash

148
00:04:49,133 --> 00:04:50,333
但它能换信任
But it can buy trust

149
00:04:50,433 --> 00:04:51,333
换机会
Buy opportunities

150
00:04:51,533 --> 00:04:53,033
换一次被认真对待
Buy being taken seriously

151
00:04:53,200 --> 00:04:55,000
换一个不那么尴尬的台阶
Buy a graceful way out

152
00:04:55,133 --> 00:04:56,933
如果你只把茶当饮料
If you only see tea as a drink

153
00:04:57,133 --> 00:04:59,700
你就会看不懂很多中国式关系
You won't understand many Chinese relationships

154
00:04:59,966 --> 00:05:01,300
明明什么都没谈
Nothing was discussed

155
00:05:01,566 --> 00:05:02,933
但关系近了一点
But the relationship got a bit closer

156
00:05:03,100 --> 00:05:04,633
明明什么都没答应
Nothing was promised

157
00:05:04,800 --> 00:05:06,433
但态度已经给出来了
But the attitude was made clear

158
00:05:06,600 --> 00:05:08,133
明明只喝了一杯茶
Only one cup of tea was shared

159
00:05:08,400 --> 00:05:11,200
但下一次开口就没那么生硬了
But next time it'll be easier to speak up

160
00:05:11,233 --> 00:05:13,933
讲到这里最重要的问题来了
Now comes the most important question

161
00:05:14,133 --> 00:05:16,233
普通人为什么要懂这件事
Why should ordinary people understand this

162
00:05:16,333 --> 00:05:18,633
因为很多人在人情往来里吃亏
Because many people lose out in social favors

163
00:05:18,933 --> 00:05:20,300
不是因为不善良
Not because they're unkind

164
00:05:20,433 --> 00:05:22,300
而是因为把成本看错了
But because they misjudge the costs

165
00:05:22,500 --> 00:05:23,633
有的人以为
Some people think

166
00:05:23,833 --> 00:05:25,766
我只是陪人喝个茶
I'm just having tea with someone

167
00:05:26,133 --> 00:05:26,933
没什么
No big deal

168
00:05:27,033 --> 00:05:28,900
但你付出的可能是时间
But what you're spending could be time

169
00:05:29,100 --> 00:05:29,933
注意力
Attention

170
00:05:30,300 --> 00:05:31,100
情绪
Emotional energy

171
00:05:31,200 --> 00:05:34,133
以及以后很难拒绝的入口
And a gateway that's hard to close later

172
00:05:34,333 --> 00:05:35,500
有的人以为
Some people think

173
00:05:35,733 --> 00:05:37,800
对方只是送我一盒茶
They just gave me a box of tea

174
00:05:38,133 --> 00:05:38,933
没什么
No big deal

175
00:05:39,033 --> 00:05:40,966
但对方真正送来的
But what they really sent

176
00:05:41,133 --> 00:05:42,633
可能是一种关系绑定
Might be a relational bind

177
00:05:42,800 --> 00:05:44,033
你一旦接了
Once you accept

178
00:05:44,300 --> 00:05:46,966
后面再拒绝就会变得更难
Saying no later becomes much harder

179
00:05:47,166 --> 00:05:48,700
还有的人以为
Others think

180
00:05:48,966 --> 00:05:50,233
自己很会做人
They're great at socializing

181
00:05:50,400 --> 00:05:51,600
到处喝茶
Drinking tea everywhere

182
00:05:51,800 --> 00:05:52,900
到处应酬
Socializing everywhere

183
00:05:53,033 --> 00:05:54,366
到处给面子
Giving face to everyone

184
00:05:54,533 --> 00:05:55,900
结果最后发现
Only to find in the end

185
00:05:56,133 --> 00:05:57,633
所有人都认识一点
They know everyone a little

186
00:05:57,800 --> 00:06:00,366
但没有一个关系真的能托住你
But no single relationship can truly support them

187
00:06:00,500 --> 00:06:02,300
这就是关系里的错觉
This is the illusion of relationships

188
00:06:02,400 --> 00:06:04,300
你以为热闹就是资源
You think busyness means resources

189
00:06:04,433 --> 00:06:06,633
其实很多热闹只是消耗
But much of that busyness is just消耗

190
00:06:06,800 --> 00:06:09,933
你以为认识很多人就是有人脉
You think knowing many people means having connections

191
00:06:10,166 --> 00:06:13,233
其实真正的人脉不是你认识谁
But real connections aren't about who you know

192
00:06:13,366 --> 00:06:16,100
而是谁愿意在关键时刻
It's about who's willing at a crucial moment

193
00:06:16,166 --> 00:06:18,133
为你承担一点成本
To bear some cost for you

194
00:06:18,233 --> 00:06:19,533
这句话很现实
This is a realistic point

195
00:06:19,633 --> 00:06:20,766
也很有用
And a very useful one

196
00:06:20,900 --> 00:06:22,333
判断一段关系
To judge a relationship

197
00:06:22,366 --> 00:06:25,200
不要只看对方会不会说好听话
Don't just look at whether they say nice things

198
00:06:25,400 --> 00:06:27,833
也不要只看他有没有请你喝茶
Or whether they invite you for tea

199
00:06:27,966 --> 00:06:31,500
要看他愿不愿意为这段关系付出真实成本
Look at whether they're willing to pay real costs for this relationship

200
00:06:31,700 --> 00:06:33,500
愿不愿意给你时间
Willing to give you time

201
00:06:33,633 --> 00:06:35,433
愿不愿意帮你确认信息
Willing to help verify information for you

202
00:06:35,633 --> 00:06:37,700
愿不愿意在你不在场的时候
Willing to speak up

203
00:06:37,933 --> 00:06:39,333
说一句公道话
When you're not around

204
00:06:39,566 --> 00:06:41,600
愿不愿意在你需要的时候
Willing to take on some trouble

205
00:06:41,766 --> 00:06:43,000
承担一点麻烦
When you need them

206
00:06:43,133 --> 00:06:45,966
这些东西才是关系的真实价格
These are the real prices of a relationship

207
00:06:46,133 --> 00:06:47,400
茶只是入口
Tea is just the entry point

208
00:06:47,566 --> 00:06:48,533
不是答案
Not the answer

209
00:06:48,733 --> 00:06:51,133
所以普通人最该警惕的
So what ordinary people should watch out for most

210
00:06:51,233 --> 00:06:52,700
不是不懂社交
Isn't not knowing how to socialize

211
00:06:52,900 --> 00:06:55,900
而是把所有喝茶饭局寒暄
It's mistaking all the tea dinners and pleasantries

212
00:06:55,900 --> 00:06:57,833
都误以为是有效关系
For genuine relationships

213
00:06:57,866 --> 00:06:58,666
不是
That's wrong

214
00:06:58,933 --> 00:07:01,566
有些茶喝完关系更清楚了
Some tea sessions make relationships clearer

215
00:07:01,700 --> 00:07:05,200
有些茶喝完只是多了一次消耗
Others are just one more drain

216
00:07:05,400 --> 00:07:06,600
有些茶喝完
After some tea

217
00:07:06,600 --> 00:07:08,600
你知道这个人可以继续往来
You know this person is worth keeping in touch with

218
00:07:08,933 --> 00:07:11,733
有些茶喝完你反而该离远一点
After others you should actually keep your distance

219
00:07:11,833 --> 00:07:13,766
关系不是越多越好
Relationships aren't about quantity

220
00:07:13,966 --> 00:07:15,766
关系是越清楚越好
They're about clarity

221
00:07:15,933 --> 00:07:18,433
一杯茶真正该帮你判断的
What a cup of tea should really help you judge

222
00:07:18,433 --> 00:07:20,233
不是对方茶叶贵不贵
Isn't whether their tea is expensive

223
00:07:20,366 --> 00:07:23,733
而是这段关系到底有没有真实价值
But whether this relationship has real value

224
00:07:23,800 --> 00:07:27,300
所以最后普通人怎么用好这杯茶
So finally how should ordinary people use this cup of tea

225
00:07:27,533 --> 00:07:29,166
不是让你变得圆滑
It's not about becoming slick

226
00:07:29,366 --> 00:07:31,233
也不是让你学会讨好
Or learning to flatter

227
00:07:31,433 --> 00:07:34,566
而是让你学会在关系里看懂三件事
It's about learning to see three things in relationships

228
00:07:34,700 --> 00:07:37,700
第一看对方到底在交换什么
First see what the other person is really exchanging

229
00:07:37,800 --> 00:07:40,333
有人请你喝茶是为了叙旧
Some invite you for tea to catch up

230
00:07:40,500 --> 00:07:42,933
有人请你喝茶是为了合作
Some invite you to discuss business

231
00:07:43,133 --> 00:07:44,400
有人请你喝茶
Some invite you

232
00:07:44,600 --> 00:07:46,600
是为了试探你能不能帮忙
To test if you can do them a favor

233
00:07:46,833 --> 00:07:48,100
有人请你喝茶
Some invite you

234
00:07:48,400 --> 00:07:50,533
只是想把他的压力转给你
Just to dump their stress on you

235
00:07:50,633 --> 00:07:52,966
你不要只听他说什么
Don't just listen to what they say

236
00:07:53,133 --> 00:07:56,633
你要看这杯茶之后他想让你做什么
Look at what they want you to do after the tea

237
00:07:56,833 --> 00:07:59,633
如果喝完茶以后你越来越轻松
If you feel lighter after tea

238
00:07:59,966 --> 00:08:01,533
这段关系可能是滋养
This relationship might be nourishing

239
00:08:01,633 --> 00:08:04,800
如果喝完茶以后你越来越有负担
If you feel more burdened after tea

240
00:08:04,966 --> 00:08:07,166
这段关系可能是在向你收费
This relationship might be charging you

241
00:08:07,400 --> 00:08:11,033
第二看自己愿意付出多少成本
Second see how much you're willing to pay

242
00:08:11,233 --> 00:08:12,833
关系不是不能维护
Relationships aren't impossible to maintain

243
00:08:13,033 --> 00:08:14,633
但你要知道边界
But you need to know your boundaries

244
00:08:14,833 --> 00:08:16,366
你愿意给时间
You'll give time

245
00:08:16,566 --> 00:08:18,366
但不一定要给承诺
But don't have to give promises

246
00:08:18,533 --> 00:08:20,200
你愿意听对方说完
You'll hear them out

247
00:08:20,433 --> 00:08:22,533
但不一定要替对方承担后果
But don't have to bear the consequences for them

248
00:08:22,633 --> 00:08:24,166
你愿意给面子
You'll give face

249
00:08:24,300 --> 00:08:26,700
但不能把自己的判断也交出去
But can't hand over your own judgment

250
00:08:26,833 --> 00:08:29,900
真正成熟的社交不是见谁都热情
Truly mature socializing isn't being warm to everyone

251
00:08:30,033 --> 00:08:32,600
而是知道哪些关系值得加温
It's knowing which relationships are worth investing in

252
00:08:32,766 --> 00:08:35,033
哪些关系保持礼貌就够了
And which only need politeness

253
00:08:35,200 --> 00:08:38,733
第三把茶变成筛选关系的工具
Third turn tea into a tool for screening relationships

254
00:08:38,900 --> 00:08:41,300
一杯茶不一定要谈成什么
A cup of tea doesn't have to lead to anything

255
00:08:41,433 --> 00:08:43,166
它可以帮你观察一个人
It can help you observe someone

256
00:08:43,400 --> 00:08:44,900
看他是不是只讲自己
See if they only talk about themselves

257
00:08:45,133 --> 00:08:46,966
看他会不会尊重你的时间
See if they respect your time

258
00:08:47,100 --> 00:08:48,700
看他能不能把话说清楚
See if they can express themselves clearly

259
00:08:48,800 --> 00:08:50,933
看他有没有把你当成一个工具
See if they treat you as a tool

260
00:08:51,033 --> 00:08:53,233
很多关系不需要吵翻
Many relationships don't need to blow up

261
00:08:53,400 --> 00:08:55,200
一杯茶就够你看明白
One cup of tea is enough to see through them

262
00:08:55,366 --> 00:08:56,566
所以回到开头
So back to the beginning

263
00:08:56,766 --> 00:08:59,600
一杯茶为什么能讲透中国人的社交货币
Why can one cup of tea explain Chinese social currency

264
00:08:59,933 --> 00:09:01,766
因为它从来不只是饮料
Because it was never just a drink

265
00:09:02,000 --> 00:09:03,766
它是一种很温和的报价
It's a very gentle price quote

266
00:09:03,966 --> 00:09:05,400
报价的是时间
The price is time

267
00:09:05,566 --> 00:09:07,233
报价的是面子
The price is face

268
00:09:07,366 --> 00:09:08,800
报价的是信任
The price is trust

269
00:09:08,933 --> 00:09:11,366
报价的是以后还能不能开口
The price is whether you can still ask for things later

270
00:09:11,600 --> 00:09:14,433
会喝茶的人不是最会应酬的人
Someone who knows tea isn't the best at socializing

271
00:09:14,600 --> 00:09:16,733
而是最清楚关系价格的人
They're the ones who know the price of relationships best

272
00:09:16,833 --> 00:09:18,400
他知道什么时候该坐下来
They know when to sit down

273
00:09:18,633 --> 00:09:20,000
什么时候该起身
When to stand up

274
00:09:20,233 --> 00:09:22,133
什么时候该接这杯茶
When to accept the tea

275
00:09:22,333 --> 00:09:25,000
什么时候该把杯子轻轻推回去
When to gently push the cup back

276
00:09:25,166 --> 00:09:28,433
茶桌上最重要的不是你懂多少茶
The most important thing at a tea table isn't how much you know about tea

277
00:09:28,733 --> 00:09:30,166
而是你懂不懂
It's whether you understand

278
00:09:30,333 --> 00:09:32,000
有些关系值得慢慢泡
Some relationships are worth brewing slowly

279
00:09:32,200 --> 00:09:34,833
有些关系喝一口就该放下
Some should be set down after one sip

280
00:09:35,000 --> 00:09:36,733
关注像素呼吸
Follow Pixel Breathing

281
00:09:36,933 --> 00:09:37,733
下一条
Next episode

282
00:09:37,800 --> 00:09:40,900
我们继续用一件你每天见过的东西
We'll keep using something you see every day

283
00:09:41,400 --> 00:09:44,500
讲透一个你没看懂的社会规则
To explain a social rule you haven't figured out

284
00:09:44,600 --> 00:09:46,333
我们聊一碗米饭
Let's talk about a bowl of rice

285
00:09:46,533 --> 00:09:49,133
它最反直觉的地方在于
The most counterintuitive thing about it

286
00:09:49,333 --> 00:09:50,700
米饭不是食物
Is that rice isn't food

287
00:09:50,800 --> 00:09:54,333
它是中国人对确定性最朴素的想象
It's the Chinese people's most basic imagination of certainty

288
00:09:54,533 --> 00:09:55,600
我们下期见
See you next time
